IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-part16-prisoners-and-entry.l4 -- sections 527 to 529.5 of the Criminal Code (Canada): procuring the attendance of a prisoner (s 527), endorsement of a warrant (s 528) and the powers to enter a
-- dwelling-house to carry out an arrest (ss 529 to 529.5). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text;
-- nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a "may" whose gate is "where", "when" or
-- "on" answers JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) and is counted in the fork register; a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails; a bar whose subject is an authorization or order that
-- does not exist answers NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c)).
-- The terms of section 2 that these sections turn on are asked as inputs named `s 2 <term>: ...` (PLAN.md section 4); "prison" can be NOTHING in the keel, so it is a MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through.
-- "An indictable offence" is tested through s 493.01 (scope assumed: Part XVI).

§ `Section 527 -- Procuring the attendance of a prisoner`

-- 527 (1) "A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order in writing that a person who is confined in a prison be brought before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the
-- prisoner is required to attend, from day to day as may be necessary, if (a) the applicant for the order sets out the facts of the case in an affidavit and produces the warrant, if any; and (b) the judge is
-- satisfied that the ends of justice require that an order be made."
-- src:11764 | 527 (1) A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order in writing that a person who is confined in a prison be brought before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the prisoner is required to attend, from day to day as may be necessary, if
-- src:11765 | (a) the applicant for the order sets out the facts of the case in an affidavit and produces the warrant, if any; and
-- src:11766 | (b) the judge is satisfied that the ends of justice require that an order be made.
@ref s 527(1) (src:11764-11766)
GIVEN `the person who would make the order is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 prison: the place where the person is confined is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant for the order sets out the facts of the case in an affidavit and produces the warrant, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the ends of justice require that an order be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(1) the judge may order in writing that a person who is confined in a prison be brought before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 prison: the place where the person is confined is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a person who is confined in a prison" (the keel's `s 2 prison` is not covered for this place)
        IF NOT `the person who would make the order is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order in writing"
        IF `s 2 prison: the place where the person is confined is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is confined in a prison" (the power is for a person confined in a prison)
        IF `the applicant for the order sets out the facts of the case in an affidavit and produces the warrant, if any` AND `the judge is satisfied that the ends of justice require that an order be made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may order in writing ... if (a) the applicant ... sets out the facts of the case in an affidavit and produces the warrant, if any; and (b) the judge is satisfied that the ends of justice require that an order be made" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- 527 (2) "A provincial court judge has the same powers for the purposes of subsection (1) or (7) as a judge has under that subsection where the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which
-- the provincial court judge has jurisdiction."
-- src:11768 | (2) A provincial court judge has the same powers for the purposes of subsection (1) or (7) as a judge has under that subsection where the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the provincial court judge has jurisdiction.
@ref s 527(2) (src:11768)
GIVEN `the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the provincial court judge has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(2) a provincial court judge has the same powers for the purposes of subsection (1) or (7) as a judge has under that subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the provincial court judge has jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person whose attendance is required is within the province in which the provincial court judge has jurisdiction" (a "where" gate on a grant of powers: ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

-- 527 (3) "An order that is made under subsection (1) or (2) shall be addressed to the person who has custody of the prisoner, and on receipt thereof that person shall (a) deliver the prisoner to any person who is
-- named in the order to receive him; or (b) bring the prisoner before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, on payment of his reasonable charges in respect thereof."
-- src:11770 | (3) An order that is made under subsection (1) or (2) shall be addressed to the person who has custody of the prisoner, and on receipt thereof that person shall
-- src:11771 | (a) deliver the prisoner to any person who is named in the order to receive him; or
-- src:11772 | (b) bring the prisoner before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, on payment of his reasonable charges in respect thereof.
@ref s 527(3) (src:11770-11772)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(3) the order must be addressed to the person who has custody of the prisoner` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order that is made under subsection (1) or (2) shall be addressed to the person who has custody of the prisoner"

@ref s 527(3)(a) (src:11771)
GIVEN `the person who has custody of the prisoner has received the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order names a person to receive the prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(3)(a) the person who has custody of the prisoner must deliver the prisoner to the person named in the order to receive the prisoner, or do what paragraph (b) requires` MEANS
    IF `the person who has custody of the prisoner has received the order` AND `the order names a person to receive the prisoner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt thereof that person shall (a) deliver the prisoner to any person who is named in the order to receive him"

@ref s 527(3)(b) (src:11772)
GIVEN `the person who has custody of the prisoner has received the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasonable charges of the person who has custody of the prisoner have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(3)(b) the person who has custody of the prisoner must bring the prisoner before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge, or do what paragraph (a) requires` MEANS
    IF `the person who has custody of the prisoner has received the order` AND `the reasonable charges of the person who has custody of the prisoner have been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt thereof that person shall ... (b) bring the prisoner before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, on payment of his reasonable charges in respect thereof" (an "on payment" gate on a duty)

-- 527 (4) "Where a prisoner is required as a witness, the judge or provincial court judge shall direct, in the order, the manner in which the prisoner shall be kept in custody and returned to the prison from which
-- he is brought."
-- src:11774 | (4) Where a prisoner is required as a witness, the judge or provincial court judge shall direct, in the order, the manner in which the prisoner shall be kept in custody and returned to the prison from which he is brought.
@ref s 527(4) (src:11774)
GIVEN `the prisoner is required as a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(4) the judge or provincial court judge must direct in the order the manner in which the prisoner is to be kept in custody and returned to the prison` MEANS
    IF `the prisoner is required as a witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a prisoner is required as a witness, the judge or provincial court judge shall direct, in the order, the manner in which the prisoner shall be kept in custody and returned to the prison from which he is brought"

-- 527 (5) "If the appearance of a prisoner is required for the purposes of subsection (1), the judge or provincial court judge shall give appropriate directions in the order with respect to the manner in which the
-- prisoner is (a) to be kept in custody, if he is ordered to stand trial; or (b) to be returned, if he is discharged on a preliminary inquiry or if he is acquitted of the charge against him."
-- src:11776 | (5) If the appearance of a prisoner is required for the purposes of subsection (1), the judge or provincial court judge shall give appropriate directions in the order with respect to the manner in which the prisoner is
-- src:11777 | (a) to be kept in custody, if he is ordered to stand trial; or
-- src:11778 | (b) to be returned, if he is discharged on a preliminary inquiry or if he is acquitted of the charge against him.
@ref s 527(5) (src:11776-11778)
GIVEN `the appearance of the prisoner is required for the purposes of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(5) the judge or provincial court judge must give appropriate directions in the order with respect to the manner in which the prisoner is to be kept in custody or returned` MEANS
    IF `the appearance of the prisoner is required for the purposes of subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the appearance of a prisoner is required for the purposes of subsection (1), the judge or provincial court judge shall give appropriate directions in the order"

@ref s 527(5)(a) and (b) (src:11777-11778)
DECLARE `s 527(5) the direction the order must give` IS ONE OF
    `s 527(5)(a) the prisoner is to be kept in custody`
    `s 527(5)(b) the prisoner is to be returned`
    `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`

@ref s 527(5)(a) and (b) (src:11777-11778)
GIVEN decision IS A `Decision on the charge`
GIVETH A `s 527(5) the direction the order must give`
`s 527(5) the direction for the decision on the charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `an order to stand trial` THEN `s 527(5)(a) the prisoner is to be kept in custody`
    WHEN `a discharge at the preliminary inquiry` THEN `s 527(5)(b) the prisoner is to be returned`
    WHEN `an acquittal` THEN `s 527(5)(b) the prisoner is to be returned`
    WHEN `a finding of guilt` THEN `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) name the order to stand trial, the discharge on a preliminary inquiry and the acquittal, and do not say "only"
    WHEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): as above
    WHEN `a verdict of unfit to stand trial` THEN `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): as above
    WHEN `a stay of proceedings` THEN `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): as above
    WHEN `a withdrawal of the charge` THEN `s 527(5) the paragraphs give no direction for the decision`   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): as above

-- 527 (6) "Sections 718.3 and 743.1 apply where a prisoner to whom this section applies is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge."
-- src:11780 | (6) Sections 718.3 and 743.1 apply where a prisoner to whom this section applies is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge.
@ref s 527(6) (src:11780)
GIVEN section IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a prisoner to whom this section applies is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(6) the section applies where the prisoner is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (section's section EQUALS 718.3 OR section's section EQUALS 743.1) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Sections 718.3 and 743.1 apply" (the text does not say "only"; another section is not covered)
        IF `a prisoner to whom this section applies is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "apply where a prisoner to whom this section applies is convicted and sentenced to imprisonment" (a "where" gate: ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

-- 527 (7) "On application by the prosecutor, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may, if a prisoner or a person in the custody of a peace officer consents in writing, order the transfer of the
-- prisoner or other person to the custody of a peace officer named in the order for a period specified in the order, where the judge is satisfied that the transfer is required for the purpose of assisting a peace
-- officer acting in the execution of his or her duties." Three gates: "if ... consents in writing" (an "if": NOTHING when it fails, ruling of 2026-11-12), "on application by the prosecutor" and "where the judge is
-- satisfied" (an "on" and a "where": JUST FALSE, ruling (b) and (c)). When the consent is missing the answer is NOTHING whatever the other two gates say (fork F-527-7-three-gates).
-- src:11782 | (7) On application by the prosecutor, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may, if a prisoner or a person in the custody of a peace officer consents in writing, order the transfer of the prisoner or other person to the custody of a peace officer named in the order for a period specified in the order, where the judge is satisfied that the transfer is required for the purpose of assisting a peace officer acting in the execution of his or her duties.
@ref s 527(7) (src:11782)
GIVEN `the person who would make the order is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prisoner or the person in the custody of a peace officer consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the transfer is required for the purpose of assisting a peace officer acting in the execution of the peace officer's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(7) the judge may order the transfer of the prisoner or other person to the custody of a peace officer named in the order for a period specified in the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person who would make the order is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may"
        IF NOT `the prisoner or the person in the custody of a peace officer consents in writing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if a prisoner or a person in the custody of a peace officer consents in writing, order the transfer" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied for the order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction may" (an "on" gate: ruling (c) treats it as "where"; the other reading is NOTHING)
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that the transfer is required for the purpose of assisting a peace officer acting in the execution of the peace officer's duties` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the judge is satisfied that the transfer is required for the purpose of assisting a peace officer acting in the execution of his or her duties" (a "where" gate: ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

