§ `Section 528 -- Endorsement of a warrant`

-- 528 (1) "Where a warrant for the arrest or committal of an accused, in any form set out in Part XXVIII in relation thereto, cannot be executed in accordance with section 514 or 703, a justice within whose
-- jurisdiction the accused is or is believed to be shall, on application and proof on oath or by affidavit of the signature of the justice who issued the warrant, authorize the arrest of the accused within his
-- jurisdiction by making an endorsement, which may be in Form 28, on the warrant."
-- src:11790 | 528 (1) Where a warrant for the arrest or committal of an accused, in any form set out in Part XXVIII in relation thereto, cannot be executed in accordance with section 514 or 703, a justice within whose jurisdiction the accused is or is believed to be shall, on application and proof on oath or by affidavit of the signature of the justice who issued the warrant, authorize the arrest of the accused within his jurisdiction by making an endorsement, which may be in Form 28, on the warrant.
@ref s 528(1) (src:11790)
GIVEN `the warrant is a warrant for the arrest or committal of an accused in a form set out in Part XXVIII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant cannot be executed in accordance with section 514 or 703` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is one within whose jurisdiction the accused is or is believed to be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proof has been made on oath or by affidavit of the signature of the justice who issued the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(1) the justice must authorize the arrest of the accused within the justice's jurisdiction by making an endorsement on the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is a warrant for the arrest or committal of an accused in a form set out in Part XXVIII`
        AND `the warrant cannot be executed in accordance with section 514 or 703`
        AND `the justice is one within whose jurisdiction the accused is or is believed to be`
        AND `an application has been made`
        AND `proof has been made on oath or by affidavit of the signature of the justice who issued the warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a warrant for the arrest or committal of an accused, in any form set out in Part XXVIII in relation thereto, cannot be executed in accordance with section 514 or 703, a justice within whose jurisdiction the accused is or is believed to be shall, on application and proof on oath or by affidavit of the signature of the justice who issued the warrant, authorize the arrest"

@ref s 528(1) Form 28 (src:11790)
GIVEN `the endorsement is in Form 28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(1) the endorsement may be in Form 28` MEANS
    IF `the endorsement is in Form 28`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an endorsement, which may be in Form 28" (the text permits Form 28 and does not say what another form is)

-- 528 (1.1) "A copy of an affidavit or warrant submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of subsection (1)."
-- src:11792 | (1.1) A copy of an affidavit or warrant submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of subsection (1).
