        IF NOT `the peace officer enters the dwelling-house without a warrant under section 529.3` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer who enters a dwelling-house without a warrant under section 529.3 may not enter the dwelling-house without prior announcement" (the bar is for an entry under section 529.3)
        IF `the peace officer has, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to suspect that prior announcement of the entry would expose the peace officer or any other person to imminent bodily harm or death`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not enter the dwelling-house without prior announcement unless the peace officer has, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, (a) reasonable grounds to suspect that prior announcement of the entry would expose the peace officer or any other person to imminent bodily harm or death"
        IF `the peace officer has, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to believe that prior announcement of the entry would result in the imminent loss or imminent destruction of evidence relating to the commission of an offence`
            AND `s 493.01 the offence is treated as an indictable offence` `the offence the evidence relates to`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the peace officer has, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, ... (b) reasonable grounds to believe that prior announcement of the entry would result in the imminent loss or imminent destruction of evidence relating to the commission of an indictable offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 529.5 "An application for a warrant under section 529.1 or an authorization under section 529 or 529.4 may be submitted, and the warrant or authorization may be issued, by a means of telecommunication, and
-- section 487.1 applies for those purposes with any necessary modifications."
